      "text": "Step 1: Expand the equation $(x - 5)^2 = 9$ by using the binomial theorem.\n(x - 5)^2 = x^2 - 10x + 25\n\nStep 2: Set the equation to zero by subtracting 9 from both sides.\nx^2 - 10x + 25 - 9 = 0\nx^2 - 10x + 16 = 0\n\nStep 3: Factor the quadratic equation x^2 - 10x + 16 = 0 to find the roots.\n(x - 2)(x - 8) = 0\n\nStep 4: Solve for x by setting each factor equal to zero.\nx - 2 = 0 => x = 2\nx - 8 = 0 => x = 8\n\nStep 5: Find the sum of the roots by adding them together.\n2 + 8 = 10\n\nThe sum of the roots of the equation $(x - 5)^2 = 9$ is $\\boxed{10}$.",
