    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) and find the sum of its roots, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the given equation:**\n   \\[\n   (x - 5)^2 = 9\n   \\]\n\n2. **Solve for \\(x\\) by taking the square root of both sides:**\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{(x - 5)^2} = \\sqrt{9}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplify the square roots:**\n   \\[\n   |x - 5| = 3\n   \\]\n\n4. **Consider the absolute value equation \\(|x - 5| = 3\\):**\n   This equation gives us two cases to solve:\n   \\[\n   x - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve each case separately:**\n   - For \\(x - 5 = 3\\):\n     \\[\n     x = 3 + 5 = 8\n     \\]\n   - For \\(x - 5 = -3\\):\n     \\[\n     x = -3 + 5 = 2\n     \\]\n\n6. **Identify the roots of the equation:**\n   The roots are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\n7. **Sum the roots:**\n   \\[\n   8 + 2 = 10\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
