      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\), we first need to solve the equation for \\(x\\).\n\nStarting with the given equation:\n\\[\n(x - 5)^2 = 9\n\\]\nwe take the square root of both sides to eliminate the square:\n\\[\nx - 5 = \\pm 3\n\\]\nThis gives us two separate equations to solve:\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n\\]\nSolving each equation separately, we get:\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\implies x = 8\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 5 = -3 \\implies x = 2\n\\]\nSo, the solutions to the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\) are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\). The roots of the equation are \\(8\\) and \\(2\\).\n\nThe sum of the roots is:\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\nTherefore, the sum of the roots of the equation is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
